# [VAR] M10 THE ACCEPT-SIDE RECEIPT for `var` and `var-unset` (the module's
# two `all-readers` rows), `block_kinds_accept.rxtin`'s own shape one
# production over: this file's own REFUSAL fixtures prove the three legs
# agree on what to REJECT, and this is what proves they agree on what to
# ACCEPT, headless -- the population every corpus file is in.
#
# BOTH SPELLINGS AND BOTH STATES IN ONE BLOCK, because block-scoped and
# repeatable is the production's whole shape: a block binds as many variables
# as its pattern mentions, one line each, and UNSET and EMPTY are two
# different states the format has to be able to tell apart.
pattern ^${a}${b}${c}$
features vars
var a "x"
var b ""
var-unset c
m "x" 0 1
